-- title:
--   Chart automorphism from an algebra automorphism congruent to the identity
-- statement:
--   Let $B'$ and $B_1$ be commutative rings with $B_1$ a $B'$-algebra whose structure map $B' \to B_1$ is surjective. Let $f \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} B'$ and $f_1 \colon X_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$ be morphisms of schemes and $g \colon X_1 \to X$ a morphism such that the square with sides $g$, $f_1$, $f$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $B' \to B_1$ is a pullback square. Let $U$ be an open subscheme of $X$ which is affine, and regard $N = \Gamma(X,U)$ as a $B'$-algebra through the composite of the inverse of $\Gamma\operatorname{Spec}$-iso for $B'$ with the component $f^{\#} \colon \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} B', \top) \to \Gamma(X,U)$ of $f$. Let $\varphi \colon N \to N$ be a $B'$-algebra automorphism such that $\varphi(x) - x$ lies, for every $x \in N$, in the ideal of $N$ generated by the image of $\ker(B' \to B_1)$. Then there is an isomorphism $\alpha$ of the scheme $U$ with itself such that: composing $\alpha$ with the canonical isomorphism $U \cong \operatorname{Spec} N$ gives the same morphism as composing that isomorphism with $\operatorname{Spec}(\varphi)$; composing $\alpha$ with the open immersion $U \to X$ followed by $f$ gives $U \to X$ followed by $f$; and the restriction $g \mid_U \colon g^{-1}(U) \to U$ followed by $\alpha$ equals $g \mid_U$.
--
--   This is the passage from ring-theoretic to geometric data on an affine chart: an automorphism of the chart's coordinate ring over the base, congruent to the identity modulo the kernel ideal of a surjection $B' \to B_1$, is realised as an automorphism of the chart over $\operatorname{Spec} B'$ which is the identity on the fibre over $\operatorname{Spec} B_1$. It is used in the construction of deformations glued from two affine charts, where such chart automorphisms are needed on the overlap compatibly with the reduction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_iso_comp_isoSpec_hom_eq_of_algEquiv_of_sub_mem.lean

